Ezechiel	Eze	31	10	1	And I saw and behold in the firmament that was over the heads of the cherubims, there appeared over them as it were the sapphire stone, as the appearance of the likeness of a throne.
Ezechiel	Eze	31	10	2	And he spoke to the man, that was clothed with linen, and said: Go in between the wheels that are under the cherubims and fill thy hand with the coals of fire that are between the cherubims, and pour them out upon the city. And he went in, in my sight:
Ezechiel	Eze	31	10	3	And the cherubims stood on the right side of the house, when the man went in, and a cloud filled the inner court.
Ezechiel	Eze	31	10	4	And the glory of the Lord was lifted up from above the cherub to the threshold of the house: and the house was filled with the cloud, and the court was filled with the brightness of the glory of the Lord.
Ezechiel	Eze	31	10	5	And the sound of the wings of the cherubims was heard even to the outward court as the voice of God Almighty speaking.
Ezechiel	Eze	31	10	6	And when he had commanded the man that was clothed with linen, saying: Take fire from the midst of the wheels that are between the cherubims: he went in and stood beside the wheel.
Ezechiel	Eze	31	10	7	And one cherub stretched out his arm from the midst of the cherubims to the fire that was between the cherubims: and he took, and put it into the hands of him that was clothed with linen: who took it and went forth.
