1 Machabees	1Mac	45	8	1	Now Judas heard of the fame of the Romans, that they are powerful and strong, and willingly agree to all things that are requested of them: and that whosoever have come to them, they have made amity with them, and that they are mighty in power.
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	8	2	And they heard of their battles, and their noble acts, which they had done in Galatia, how they conquered them, and brought them under tribute:
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	8	3	And how great things they had done in the land of Spain, and that they had brought under their power the mines of silver and of gold that are there, and had gotten possession of all the place by their counsel and patience:
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	8	4	And had conquered places that were very far off from them, and kings that came against them from the ends of the earth, and had overthrown them with great slaughter: and the rest pay them tribute every year.
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	8	5	And that they had defeated in battle Philip, and Perses the king of the Ceteans, and the rest that had borne arms against them, and had conquered them:
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	8	6	And how Antiochus the great king of Asia, who went to fight against them, having a hundred and twenty elephants, with horsemen, and chariots, and a very great army, was routed by them:
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	8	7	And how they took him alive, and appointed to him, that both he and they that should reign after him, should pay a great tribute, and that he should give hostages, and that which was agreed upon,
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	8	8	And the country of the Indians, and of the Medes, and of the Lydians, some of their best provinces: and those which they had taken from them they gave to king Eumenes.
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	8	9	And that they who were in Greece had a mind to go and to destroy them: and they had knowledge thereof,
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	8	10	And they sent a general against them, and fought with them, and many of them were slain, and they carried away their wives and their children captives, and spoiled them, and took possession of their land, and threw down their walls, and brought them to be their servants unto this day.
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	8	11	And the other kingdoms, and islands, that at any time had resisted them, they had destroyed and brought under their power.
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	8	12	But with their friends, and such as relied upon them, they kept amity, and had conquered kingdoms that were near, and that were far off: for all that heard their name, were afraid of them.
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	8	13	That whom they had a mind to help to a kingdom, those reigned: and whom they would, they deposed from a kingdom: and they were greatly exalted.
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	8	14	And none of all these wore a crown, or was clothed in purple, to be magnified thereby.
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	8	15	And that they made themselves a senate house, and consulted daily three hundred and twenty men, that sat in council always for the people, that they might do the things that were right.
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	8	16	And that they committed their government to one man every year, to rule over all their country, and they all obey one, and there is no envy, nor jealousy amongst them.
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	8	17	So Judas chose Eupolemus the son of John, the son of Jacob, and Jason the son of Eleazar, and he sent them to Rome to make a league of amity and confederacy with them.
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	8	18	And that they might take off from them the yoke of the Grecians, for they saw that they oppressed the kingdom of Israel with servitude.
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	8	19	And they went to Rome, a very long journey, and they entered into the senate house, and said:
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	8	20	Judas Machabeus, and his brethren, and the people of the Jews have sent us to you, to make alliance and peace with you, and that we may be registered your confederates and friends.
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	8	21	And the proposal was pleasing in their sight.
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	8	22	And this is the copy of the writing that they wrote back again, graven in tables of brass, and sent to Jerusalem, that it might be with them there for a memorial of the peace and alliance.
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	8	23	GOOD SUCCESS BE TO THE ROMANS, and to the people of the Jews, by sea and by land for ever: and far be the sword and enemy from them.
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	8	24	But if there come first any war upon the Romans, or any of their confederates, in all their dominions:
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	8	25	The nation of the Jews shall help them according as the time shall direct, with all their heart:
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	8	26	Neither shall they give them, whilst they are fighting, or furnish them with wheat, or arms, or money, or ships, as it hath seemed good to the Romans: and they shall obey their orders, without taking any thing of them.
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	8	27	In like manner also if war shall come first upon the nation of the Jews, the Romans shall help them with all their heart, according as the time shall permit them.
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	8	28	And there shall not be given to them that come to their aid, either wheat, or arms, or money, or ships, as it hath seemed good to the Romans: and they shall observe their orders without deceit.
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	8	29	According to these articles did the Romans covenant with the people of the Jews.
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	8	30	And if after this one party or the other shall have a mind to add to these articles, or take away anything, they may do it at their pleasure: and whatsoever they shall add, or take away, shall be ratified.
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	8	31	Moreover concerning the evils that Demetrius the king hath done against them, we have written to him, saying: Why hast thou made thy yoke heavy upon our friends, and allies, the Jews?
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	8	32	If therefore they come again to us complaining of thee, we will do them justice, and will make war against thee by sea and land.
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	9	1	In the mean time when Demetrius heard that Nicanor and his army were fallen in battle, he sent again Bacchides and Alcimus into Judea; and the right wing of his army with them.
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	9	2	And they took the road that leadeth to Galgal, and they camped in Masaloth, which is in Arabella: and they made themselves masters of it, and slew many people.
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	9	3	In the first month of the hundred and fifty-second year they brought the army to Jerusalem:
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	9	4	And they arose, and went to Berea with twenty thousand men, and two thousand horsemen.
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	9	5	Now Judas had pitched his tents in Laisa, and three thousand chosen men with him:
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	9	6	And they saw the multitude of the army that they were many, and they were seized with great fear: and many withdrew themselves out of the camp, and there remained of them no more than eight hundred men.
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	9	7	And Judas saw that his army slipped away, and the battle pressed upon him, and his heart was cast down: because he had not time to gather them together, and he was discouraged.
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	9	8	Then he said to them that remained: Let us arise, and go against our enemies, if we may be able to fight against them.
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	9	9	But they dissuaded him, saying: We shall not be able, but let us save our lives now, and return to our brethren, and then we will fight against them: for we are but few.
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	9	10	Then Judas said: God forbid we should do this thing, and flee away from them: but if our time be come, let us die manfully for our brethren, and let us not stain our glory.
1 Machabees	1Mac	45	9	11	And the army removed out of the camp, and they stood over against them: and the horsemen were divided into two troops, and the slingers, and the archers went before the army, and they that were in the front were all men of valour.
